; 50-tex.kurt

; `tex SYMBOL TEXT` says how a symbol is written in LaTeX. It changes nothing in the proof:
; it is only used by `kurt --latex FILE` and `kurt --markdown FILE`, which write the checked
; proof as a document. `$1`, `$2`, ... are the places of the arguments.

load logic
const alpha, beta
tex alpha \alpha
tex beta \beta

prop P
arity P 2
tex P \mathrm{P}($1, $2)

alpha = alpha
P alpha beta implies P alpha beta

; try: kurt --latex keywords/50-tex.kurt    (writes keywords/50-tex.tex)
